# 📚 Cybersecurity Learning Resources

Beginner-friendly places to learn and practise legally.

## 🏁 Practice Platforms (legal & beginner-friendly)

| Resource | Best for |
|----------|----------|
| [picoCTF](https://picoctf.org/) | Beginner CTF challenges across all categories, with a learning-oriented design |
| [OverTheWire](https://overthewire.org/wargames/) | Linux command-line skills (start with *Bandit*) |
| [TryHackMe](https://tryhackme.com/) | Guided rooms and learning paths |
| [Hack The Box](https://www.hackthebox.com/) | Intermediate to advanced labs |
| [CTFlearn](https://ctflearn.com/) | Community-made beginner challenges |
| [CryptoHack](https://cryptohack.org/) | Learning cryptography through puzzles |
| [PortSwigger Web Security Academy](https://portswigger.net/web-security) | Free, in-depth web security training |

## 📖 Guides & References

- [CTF 101](https://ctf101.org/) — introduction to CTF concepts and categories
- [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/) — the most common web application risks
- [OWASP Cheat Sheet Series](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/) — practical defensive guidance
- [Linux Journey](https://linuxjourney.com/) — learn Linux from scratch
- [Explain Shell](https://explainshell.com/) — paste a command to get each part explained
- [Wireshark User Guide](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/) — packet analysis

## 🛠️ Online Tools

- [CyberChef](https://gchq.github.io/CyberChef/) — encoding, decoding, crypto, and data transformation
- [dCode](https://www.dcode.fr/en) — cipher identifier and solvers
- [Aperi'Solve](https://www.aperisolve.com/) — online image steganography analysis
- [Wayback Machine](https://web.archive.org/) — archived web pages
- [Exiftool documentation](https://exiftool.org/) — metadata reference

## 🕵️ OSINT Learning

- [OSINT Framework](https://osintframework.com/) — directory of OSINT tools by category
- [Bellingcat's guides](https://www.bellingcat.com/resources/) — responsible open-source investigation methods

## 🎓 Courses & Certifications (to explore later)

- Google Cybersecurity Certificate
- CompTIA Security+
- eJPT (INE) — entry-level practical pentesting
- SANS Cyber Aces (free introductory material)

## ⚖️ Ethics & Law

- Only test systems you own or have **written permission** to test.
- Read each CTF's rules before starting and before publishing writeups.
- Learn about responsible disclosure: [CERT/CC guidance](https://www.kb.cert.org/vuls/guidelines/).

